To factor $x^2 - 16x + 60$, we find $a$ and $b$ such that $a+b=16$ and $ab=60$. The factors of 60 summing to 16 are 10 and 6. Since $a > b$, we have $a=10$ and $b=6$.
Calculating $3b - a$: $3(6) - 10 = 18 - 10 = 8$.

\boxed{8}
